# 2026-09-13 (gen514) — full live KB; development probes, never persisted training.
# The finite verb of a wh-question says which argument is asked: «what supports
# X?» asks the subject, «what does X support?» the object. The sentences below
# test that mechanic on the words of the prose ladder (r300) and on a relation
# verb taught by speaking; they do not claim world knowledge.

[test the subject question reaches the root relation]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!timeout 30
> Hard carbonate exoskeletons support the coral.
<~ Learned
> what supports the corals?
<~ exoskeletons
> what do hard carbonate exoskeletons support?
<~ coral
> Excess nutrients threaten coral reefs.
<~ Learned
> what threatens coral reefs?
<~ excess nutrients
> what can excess nutrients threaten?
<~ coral reefs

[test the object question does not answer the other direction]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Hard carbonate exoskeletons support the coral.
<~ Learned
# It used to answer «Hard carbonate exoskeletons.»: what supports the coral,
# to a question about what the coral supports.
> what does coral support?
<! exoskeletons

[test a declarative with a finite verb is still read, not asked]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa.
<~ Learned
> Calcium carbonate holds colonies of coral polyps together.
<~ Learned
> what holds colonies together?
<~ calcium carbonate
# The participle after the copula is not an object question («what IS a
# compass USED for?» must keep its purpose reading).
> what is a compass used for?
<~ finding north
# With the direction declared the universal frame answers too, and it must
# keep the asked type: «Class anthozoa.» is not a phylum.
> what phylum does coral belong to?
<! anthozoa
> what class does coral belong to?
<~ anthozoa

[test a relation verb taught by speaking gets its direction]
!reset
!timeout 30
> cement is a relation verb
<~ Learned
> Calcium carbonate cements coral polyps.
<~ Learned
> what cements coral polyps?
<~ calcium carbonate
# Before gen514 the frame tried both arguments and answered «calcium
# carbonate.» here too.
> what do coral polyps cement?
<! calcium carbonate
> what does calcium carbonate cement?
<~ coral polyps
> forget that cement is a relation verb
<~ no longer
> what does calcium carbonate cement?
<! coral polyps
> cement is a relation verb
<~ Learned
> what does calcium carbonate cement?
<~ coral polyps
